# The SMB2 ERROR response's body with no error data, written by hand from
# MS-SMB2 2.2.2 and 3.3.4.4: its StructureSize is 9 whatever the error data's
# length, and with nothing provided ByteCount is 0. The ninth byte is the one
# byte of ErrorData that StructureSize counts, sent as 0. The reference
# server sends these same 9 bytes after the header of frame 127 in
# test/pcap-corpus/smb-sd/reference.pcap (create_response.hex). Multi-byte
# fields are little-endian (MS-SMB2 2.2).
09 00                       # [0,2) StructureSize 9
00                          # [2]   ErrorContextCount 0
00                          # [3]   Reserved
00 00 00 00                 # [4,8) ByteCount 0
00                          # [8]   ErrorData
